.build/
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.obj
# 地图的烘焙材质色旁车（bake_map_colors.py）。一张图 7-21 MB，而且这个功能默认
# 关着（map-loader.js 的 BAKED_COLORS），没有理由跟着仓库走。
maps/optimized_obj_files/*.colors.bin
.vscode/
visualizer/outputs/
# The web app's own data: config, the SQLite library, .csz files, thumbnails,
# avatars. Anchored on purpose -- it lives under app/ now, and the repo root's
# data/ is a different thing entirely (training data).
/app/data/
# Training data / scratch datasets at the repo root.
/data/
# Smoke-test output from scripts/training_data/tasks/*.py (`python -m
# scripts.training_data.tasks.example`). Regenerated from scratch on every run.
/tmp/
# Training runs (`training/aim/train.py` 的 `train.save_dir`): checkpoint 里存了
# 参数 + AdamW 两个动量，25.9 M 的配置一份 `last.pt` 就 ~320 MB，再有一份
# `best.pt`。别进 git。
/runs/
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose: an unanchored "examples/" also matches
# visualizer/static/three/examples/, which silently blocks vendored three.js
# addons (GLTFLoader, BufferGeometryUtils) from ever being committed. Already
# tracked files ignore gitignore rules, so that breakage only appears on a
# fresh clone -- where the importmap would then 404.
/examples/
# Raw extracted CS2 assets and the Source2Viewer-CLI binary. These are Valve's
# copyrighted content (personal, non-commercial use only) plus a ~108 MB
# third-party executable -- the raw tree is GB-scale and stays out. Rebuild
# locally with tools/cs2_assets/extract_cs2_assets.py; see
# notes/research-gameassets.md.
# Anchored: an unanchored "assets/" also swallows visualizer/static/assets/,
# which IS tracked here -- it is the trimmed set the browser actually fetches,
# see the note at the bottom of this file.
/assets/
tools/Source2Viewer-CLI/

# Large binary output from the CS2 asset probes (game assets, not source).
# The scripts and the text/JSON listings next to them stay tracked.
#
# This block used to end with a blanket "*.glb" ("no GLB belongs in the repo").
# That premise died when the staged weapon models were committed -- and the
# blanket pattern was the silent kind of wrong in both directions: upstream of
# the change it would have skipped the 65 weapon GLBs without a word, and
# downstream it would skip any GLB that SHOULD be tracked (a test fixture, say).
# Same trap as the unanchored "examples/" in notes/research-gameassets.md §9.7
# bug 3. GLBs are now handled per location instead: ignored under here and under
# /assets/ (both whole directories are already excluded), visible everywhere
# else so a new one shows up in `git status` instead of vanishing.
notes/scratch/asset_probe/

# The full 137k-entry VPK listing is regenerable in ~2s with
#   Source2Viewer-CLI -i pak01_dir.vpk --vpk_list
# and the derived list_*.txt files come from inventory.py. Keep SUMMARY.md,
# which is the part actually cited by the report.
notes/scratch/asset_inventory/vpk_full_list.txt
notes/scratch/asset_inventory/list_*.txt

# Compiled Go probe binaries under notes/scratch/<probe>/ -- ~14 MB each, one
# per research probe. Build them with `go build -o <name> .` from the .go source
# that sits next to each one; the sources stay tracked.
notes/scratch/coverprobe/coverprobe
notes/scratch/fireprobe/fireprobe
notes/scratch/goprobe/probe
notes/scratch/nadeprobe/nadeprobe
notes/scratch/voxprobe/voxprobe

# Assets staged for the browser by tools/cs2_assets/install_web_assets.py.
#
# **Tracked on purpose** -- the one deliberate exception to the /assets/ rule
# above. These are Valve's copyrighted assets, and they are committed anyway
# because a clean checkout cannot rebuild them: staging needs a local CS2
# install plus the 108 MB Source2Viewer-CLI, and the extractor's --out does not
# produce the layout install_web_assets.py reads (it takes three runs with three
# different --outs). The reasoning and the damage are written up in
# notes/research-gameassets.md §9.0.1.
#
# Cost: ~300 MB, ~903 files, and binary churn on every re-extraction.
# Constraint: Steam licences this content for "personal, non-commercial use"
# only (SSA §2.A), so **this repository has to stay private** -- publishing it,
# forking it publicly, or attaching these files to a release redistributes
# Valve's assets. See notes/research-assets.md §6.
#
# Only the trimmed set the browser actually fetches lives here: 358 sprite
# frames, 68 HUD icons, 65 weapon directories. Everything raw stays ignored:
# /assets/, notes/scratch/asset_probe/, tools/Source2Viewer-CLI/.

models/